# =============================================================
# Velociraptor Custom Kernel Config Fragment
# i7-8700K (Coffee Lake) / RTX 2080 / ASUS Prime Z390-A
# =============================================================
# Applied on top of linux-zen via merge_config.sh.
# Only lists differences from zen defaults.
# Keep this file: when zen updates, re-run setup.sh to rebuild.


# --- AutoFDO + Propeller: Profile-guided optimization ---
# Both are compatible with ThinLTO and each other.
# AUTOFDO_CLANG: hot-path optimization based on perf profile.
# PROPELLER_CLANG: code layout optimization (function/basic block ordering).
# For the optimized build: pass CLANG_AUTOFDO_PROFILE via patch_pkgbuild.py.
# For Propeller: need a perf.data collected on a binary built with both flags
# enabled — do this on the next profile refresh, then also pass
# CLANG_PROPELLER_PROFILE_PREFIX to the build.
CONFIG_AUTOFDO_CLANG=y
CONFIG_PROPELLER_CLANG=y


# --- Compiler: Clang ThinLTO ---
# GCC build replaced with Clang + link-time optimisation.
# ThinLTO chosen over Full for reasonable build times (~2-3h vs 6h+).
# DKMS modules (nvidia, looking-glass, v4l2loopback, vboxhost) are
# compiled separately and are NOT affected by kernel LTO.
CONFIG_LTO_NONE=n
CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN=y

# Allow DKMS modules with BTF that doesn't match the kernel's.
# Required because DKMS compiles with GCC while the kernel uses Clang/LTO,
# producing incompatible BTF debug info. Without this, i2c_nct6793,
# v4l2loopback, and others fail to insert at early boot.
CONFIG_MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH=y


# --- CPU: trim max CPU count ---
# Zen default is 8192. i7-8700K has 12 threads; 16 leaves room for VMs.
CONFIG_NR_CPUS=16


# --- GPU: remove unused driver families ---
# Proprietary nvidia is a DKMS module and never built into the kernel.
# Nouveau, AMDGPU, and Radeon have no hardware to attach to.
CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU=n
CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU=n
CONFIG_DRM_RADEON=n
# Re-enabled 2026-08-08: was =n after a 2026-07-20 incident (EFI framebuffer
# landing on card0, NVIDIA on card1, KWin picking card0 -> Mesa llvmpipe
# software rendering at 800% CPU), on the assumption stock linux-zen doesn't
# build simpledrm either. That assumption was wrong — stock zen currently
# ships CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM=y and boots cleanly on this same hardware/driver.
# Missing simpledrm is also the confirmed root cause of a separate bug: no
# fallback console for NVIDIA's weak generic fbdev, causing broken/frozen
# VT-switch and shutdown console transitions (see memory:
# project_nvidia_vt_switch_freeze.md). Re-enabling to fix that. If the old
# llvmpipe/high-CPU symptom reappears, revert this line to =n first.
CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM=y

# Fix for the KWin-picks-wrong-GPU regression the above simpledrm re-enable caused
# (2026-08-08, ~30-round bisection across an 8-hour session — see memory:
# project_nvidia_vt_switch_freeze.md for the full story). Symptom: KWin picked simpledrm's
# card0 instead of NVIDIA's card1 at Plasma startup, glitchy/flashing desktop. Missing
# from every dmesg capture: "vgaarb: deactivate vga console" / "fbcon: ... is primary
# device" — the kernel's handoff from the firmware framebuffer to the real GPU driver
# never fired. Two independent things needed fixing, both examples of the same root
# mechanism (localmodconfig stripping something silently, with no warning):
#
# 1. VGA_SWITCHEROO (GPU-handoff coordination) `depends on (FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=n ||
#    FB=y)` — CONFIG_FB (legacy fbdev core) was being stripped since nothing visibly
#    used it at lsmod-snapshot time, silently failing VGA_SWITCHEROO's dependency.
# 2. CONFIG_I2C (base I2C bus subsystem, used for DDC/EDID display communication) was
#    ALSO being stripped for the same reason — this is what the DRM_VBOXVIDEO line below
#    actually forces on (see its comment).
#
# CONFIG_APERTURE_HELPERS is technically redundant to list here — DRM_SIMPLEDRM already
# `select`s it unconditionally, and it's a prompt-less/hidden Kconfig symbol that can't
# be forced by direct assignment anyway (same class of thing as DRM_VRAM_HELPER below).
# Left in as a documented reminder of the mechanism, not because this line does anything.
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_VGA_SWITCHEROO=y
CONFIG_APERTURE_HELPERS=y

# Confirmed via the same bisection: localmodconfig was also stripping DRM_I915 despite
# the reminder below saying not to — the iGPU is bound to vfio-pci (not i915) for the
# Windows11 VM passthrough at lsmod-snapshot time, so localmodconfig never saw it as
# "in use". Promoting from passive comment to active directive.
CONFIG_DRM_I915=m

# The other genuinely necessary piece, alongside FB/VGA_SWITCHEROO above: CONFIG_I2C
# (base I2C bus, used for DDC/EDID communication with the actual monitor — part of why
# the KWin symptom included "Could not find edid for connector" in kwin_wayland's log).
# localmodconfig was stripping it entirely for the same "nothing visibly uses it" reason.
CONFIG_I2C=y

# DRM_VBOXVIDEO=m is NOT here for VirtualBox guest support (this machine is bare metal,
# this module will never bind to anything) — it's a vehicle for CONFIG_FB_CORE, a distinct
# and more modern hidden symbol from the legacy CONFIG_FB above (drivers/video/fbdev/core/
# Kconfig — bare `tristate`, no prompt, `select VIDEO`). FB_CORE is what DRM's generic
# fbdev-emulation client actually needs to complete the vgaarb/fbcon handoff; confirmed
# absent in every broken build's .config, present only in working ones.
#
# The weird part, root-caused not just worked-around: CONFIG_DRM_KMS_HELPER (already =y
# in every build all along) ALSO does `select FB_CORE if DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION` (also already
# =y all along) — by the Kconfig graph that alone should have forced FB_CORE=y regardless
# of anything else. It never did, in any broken build. This is the same failure mode as
# APERTURE_HELPERS at the very start of this saga: conditional `select X if Y` relationships
# don't reliably re-resolve in THIS PKGBUILD's specific build order (prepare() runs
# `make localmodconfig` BEFORE `merge_config.sh`, then one final `make olddefconfig`) even
# when Y is already true. The only reliable fix pattern found: force a REAL, non-hidden
# option that selects the target unconditionally. DRM_VBOXVIDEO (`select FB_CORE if
# DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION`, same conditional form) happens to hold reliably where the other two
# paths didn't — not fully explained beyond "empirically verified across many rebuild/
# reboot cycles," likely down to Kconfig's internal processing order in a single pass.
#
# Confirmed via `grep -rln "select FB_CORE" drivers/gpu/drm/ drivers/video/` — three hits
# (drm/Kconfig's DRM_KMS_HELPER, drm/clients/Kconfig's DRM_CLIENT_LIB, video/fbdev/Kconfig).
# DRM_VBOXVIDEO reaches FB_CORE via DRM_TTM_HELPER -> FB_CORE, a fourth path, is the one that
# actually works. If a kernel version bump breaks this, re-run that grep and re-test whichever
# real (non-hidden) option reaches FB_CORE most directly.
#
# Worth a future session (not this one): try reordering prepare() so config.custom merges
# BEFORE localmodconfig, or add an extra `make olddefconfig` pass after the merge — might
# make direct selects hold without needing vehicle options like this at all. See memory:
# project_nvidia_vt_switch_freeze.md for the full investigation.
CONFIG_DRM_VBOXVIDEO=m


# --- USB: remove legacy host controllers ---
# Z390-A uses xHCI exclusively. USB 2.0 devices (keyboard, BT dongle,
# etc.) are served by xHCI's built-in transaction translator.
# EHCI/OHCI/UHCI are dead weight on any post-2012 Intel platform.
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=n
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=n
CONFIG_USB_UHCI_HCD=n


# --- WiFi: remove entire wireless stack ---
# Z390-A has no wireless hardware (ethernet-only board).
# Bluetooth uses its own btusb/btrtl stack and does NOT depend on
# cfg80211 or mac80211, so this is safe.
CONFIG_WIRELESS=n
CONFIG_CFG80211=n
CONFIG_MAC80211=n


# --- Virtualisation: remove AMD paths ---
# i7-8700K uses VMX (Intel VT-x), not AMD SVM.
# Intel IOMMU is kept — it is required for the iGPU VFIO passthrough.
CONFIG_KVM_AMD=n
CONFIG_KVM_AMD_SEV=n
CONFIG_AMD_IOMMU=n
CONFIG_AMD_MEM_ENCRYPT=n


# --- Unused hardware subsystems ---
CONFIG_FIREWIRE=n
# No FireWire ports on Z390-A

CONFIG_PARPORT=n
# No parallel port

CONFIG_BLK_DEV_FD=n
# No floppy drive

CONFIG_HAMRADIO=n
# No ham radio

CONFIG_ISDN=n
# No ISDN hardware

CONFIG_INFINIBAND=n
# No InfiniBand; mlx4.conf in modprobe.d is just a commented template


# --- Filesystems ---
# datastore (bitlk-datastore) has 0xFFFFFEFF clusters (~16TB), right at the 32-bit
# ceiling. Without this, ntfs3 log replay bails on runs near the cluster limit and
# re-marks the volume dirty, making it unmountable with ntfs3 even with force=y.
# ntfs-3g is used as a workaround in fstab until this is compiled in.
CONFIG_NTFS3_64BIT_CLUSTER=y

# Optical disc / ISO filesystems — stripped by localmodconfig (no disc in drive at snapshot time)
# UDF: Blu-ray/DVD ISOs (e.g. Kraftwerk concert ISO)
CONFIG_UDF_FS=m
# ISO 9660: standard CD/DVD filesystem, required for most ISOs
CONFIG_ISO9660_FS=m
CONFIG_JOLIET=y
CONFIG_ZISOFS=y

# SquashFS — AppImages, Flatpak, live USBs, snap
CONFIG_SQUASHFS=m
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_ZSTD=y

# EROFS — Android images, some containers
CONFIG_EROFS_FS=m


# --- CPU frequency scaling ---
# localmodconfig strips acpi_cpufreq because built-in drivers don't appear
# in lsmod. Without it and with intel_pstate failing (HWP disabled in BIOS),
# the CPU is stuck at base clock (3700 MHz) with no turbo.
# Must be built-in (=y), not module (=m) — needs to run at boot time
# before ACPI processor P-state structures are torn down.
CONFIG_X86_ACPI_CPUFREQ=y


# --- Debug info / BTF ---
# Full DWARF is required for CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF — DEBUG_INFO_REDUCED is
# mutually exclusive with BTF. BTF is needed for CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT
# (sched-ext / scx_lavd gaming scheduler). Build time cost ~20-40% more;
# installed bzImage is unaffected in size (DWARF is stripped from it).
# DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES=n: skip per-module BTF — DKMS modules are GCC-built
# and MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH=y already handles the mismatch.
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES=n
CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT=y


# --- NUMA ---
# i7-8700K is single-socket with no NUMA topology. Disabling removes
# overhead from every memory allocation path.
CONFIG_NUMA=n


# --- Thunderbolt / Cavium ARM server NICs (no hardware) ---
# Z390-A has no Thunderbolt ports. Cavium ThunderX is an ARM server NIC.
CONFIG_INTEL_WMI_THUNDERBOLT=n
CONFIG_CAVIUM_PTP=n
CONFIG_THUNDER_NIC_PF=n
CONFIG_THUNDER_NIC_VF=n
CONFIG_THUNDER_NIC_BGX=n
CONFIG_THUNDER_NIC_RGX=n


# --- Loop device ---
# Required for AppImages (eden emulator etc.) and mounting disk/ISO images.
# localmodconfig strips it if no loop devices were active at snapshot time.
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=m


# --- VMs: TUN/TAP and 9P virtio filesystem ---
# TUN: required for VPNs (WireGuard userspace, OpenVPN) and VM networking
CONFIG_TUN=m
# 9P: QEMU/KVM virtio filesystem sharing (host↔guest directory sharing)
CONFIG_NET_9P=m
CONFIG_NET_9P_VIRTIO=m
CONFIG_9P_FS=m


# --- Hardware exceptions for localmodconfig ---
# setup.sh captures lsmod.txt and localmodconfig strips everything not
# currently loaded. These devices are used regularly but may not be
# plugged in at snapshot time — restore them explicitly here.
#
# Blue Yeti mic + Roland PCR-800 MIDI keyboard (USB audio/MIDI)
CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO=m
CONFIG_SND_RAWMIDI=m
CONFIG_SND_SEQ_MIDI=m
CONFIG_SND_SEQ_MIDI_EMUL=m
CONFIG_SND_SEQ_MIDI_EVENT=m
# DualSense Edge controller (USB or Bluetooth)
CONFIG_HID_PLAYSTATION=m
# Legacy joystick interface (/dev/js*) — needed by some older games
CONFIG_JOYDEV=m
# Android devices via USB (ADB CDC-ACM mode, Galaxy S23/Tab S7+)
CONFIG_USB_ACM=m
# Windows network share access (CIFS/SMB client, for Windows PCs on LAN)
CONFIG_CIFS=m
# PCH onboard audio (ALC1220 codec, S/PDIF passthrough — see project_mpv_audio.md) and NVIDIA
# HDMI/DP audio codec support. Both went missing 2026-08-09: localmodconfig stripped them since
# audio hadn't successfully probed on this kernel in a while (a vicious cycle caused by the VFIO
# early-bind dracut config starving i915's audio-component registration — see memory:
# project_audio_hda_probe_regression.md — fixed separately, but these codec drivers still need
# restoring explicitly since localmodconfig had already stripped them by the time that was fixed).
CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_REALTEK=m
CONFIG_SND_HDA_GENERIC=m
CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI=m


# --- Network: congestion control + fair queuing ---
# BBR for better throughput under load (qbittorrent etc.); FQ qdisc pairs with it.
# Both were absent from the current kernel build — added 2026-06-15.
CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR=y
CONFIG_NET_SCH_FQ=m
CONFIG_DEFAULT_TCP_CONG="bbr"


# --- IMPORTANT: things we must NOT disable ---
# These are here as reminders — they are already enabled in zen defaults.
#
# CONFIG_KVM=m                  QEMU Windows VM
# CONFIG_KVM_INTEL=m            Intel VT-x
# CONFIG_VFIO=m                 iGPU passthrough (8086:3e92 → vfio-pci)
# CONFIG_VFIO_PCI=m             ditto
# CONFIG_VFIO_IOMMU_TYPE1=m     ditto
# CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU=y          ditto
# CONFIG_DRM_I915=m             now an ACTIVE line above (2026-08-08) — was silently
#                                stripped by localmodconfig despite this reminder;
#                                see the GPU-handoff fix comment above CONFIG_FB
# CONFIG_SND_ALOOP=m            audio loopback used for VM audio
# CONFIG_BT=m                   ASUS USB-BT500 (RTL8761BU)
# CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB=m          ditto
# CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB_RTL=y      Realtek firmware loading
# CONFIG_BT_RFCOMM=m            phone as BT storage/audio
# CONFIG_BT_BNEP=m              ditto
# CONFIG_V4L2_LOOPBACK           DroidCam virtual camera (DKMS)
# CONFIG_BTRFS_FS=y             root filesystem
# CONFIG_NTFS3_FS=m             BitLocker drives (4x)
# CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=m             BitLocker decryption
# CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=m             Ventoy USB stick
# CONFIG_TUN=m                  VPN + VM networking (WireGuard, OpenVPN, QEMU)
# CONFIG_NET_9P=m               QEMU/KVM 9P virtio filesystem sharing
# CONFIG_NET_9P_VIRTIO=m        ditto
# CONFIG_9P_FS=m                ditto
# CONFIG_E1000E=m               Intel I219-V — the only NIC
# CONFIG_IA32_EMULATION=y       Steam + 32-bit game binaries
# CONFIG_ASUS_WMI=m             Aura RGB + fan/sensor control
# CONFIG_I2C_I801=m             SMBus (disable_features handled in modprobe.d)
